00:58:14.330 --> 00:58:15.163
And those are people

00:58:15.163 --> 00:58:16.990
who are generally politically connected.

00:58:16.990 --> 00:58:20.060
And so when you say that
we should have models

00:58:20.060 --> 00:58:22.750
that point towards an endogenous level

00:58:22.750 --> 00:58:26.500
of socially optimum Political Connections,

00:58:26.500 --> 00:58:29.420
would those be positive
under certain conditions?

00:58:29.420 --> 00:58:30.253
Thank you.

00:58:30.253 --> 00:58:32.262
- Yeah, the short is yes.

00:58:32.262 --> 00:58:37.262
So basically, Political
Connection is (indistinct)-

00:58:39.700 --> 00:58:42.700
- [Man 1] Put on the mic.
- Oh sorry.

00:58:49.560 --> 00:58:54.100
We need to think about non
stationary Political Connection,

00:58:54.100 --> 00:58:58.680
for instance, bringing
private sector expertise

00:58:58.680 --> 00:59:03.680
in regulation in policy making,
but you have to be careful

00:59:05.460 --> 00:59:07.040
about conflict of interest.

00:59:07.040 --> 00:59:08.703
You have to be careful about,

00:59:12.610 --> 00:59:17.610
attempt by firms to block entry and so on.

00:59:18.600 --> 00:59:23.600
So I think private and public partnerships

00:59:24.290 --> 00:59:27.080
can be non stationary

00:59:27.080 --> 00:59:30.310
and political process exactly as you said,

00:59:30.310 --> 00:59:35.310
can be informed or can be improved

00:59:37.290 --> 00:59:40.580
by some type of connection
with private sector,

00:59:40.580 --> 00:59:45.580
but we need to find creative
way to reduce stationary,

00:59:49.280 --> 00:59:51.553
private connection,
like when we described.

00:59:54.581 --> 00:59:55.774
- [Instructor] Thank you for that.

00:59:55.774 --> 00:59:58.941
Any other questions from the audience?

