is that even in a polarized society,

01:21:32.070 --> 01:21:34.860
it's worth trying to build a consensus,

01:21:34.860 --> 01:21:36.750
even if you achieve it or not.

01:21:36.750 --> 01:21:41.750
It's worth trying to find
reasons for us to work together,

01:21:42.210 --> 01:21:46.733
to find reasons why we
should be less divided,

01:21:48.060 --> 01:21:52.220
and if the reason exists
and you are patient enough,

01:21:52.220 --> 01:21:56.963
then you can overcome those divisions.

01:21:58.220 --> 01:22:02.020
So, the point here is that ideologies,

01:22:08.420 --> 01:22:11.920
ideological differences
act like ethnic differences

01:22:16.780 --> 01:22:18.520
in many contexts,

01:22:18.520 --> 01:22:23.520
but even then there must
be institutional setting.

01:22:24.350 --> 01:22:27.340
There must be institutional innovation

01:22:28.450 --> 01:22:32.893
that try to bridge the divides.

01:22:33.850 --> 01:22:38.850
And one key element I think
is putting forward the needs

01:22:44.470 --> 01:22:48.060
for collaboration, the need
for consensus building,

01:22:48.060 --> 01:22:50.880
whether this works in
the short term or not,

01:22:50.880 --> 01:22:55.270
and I think anyway, so
that's what I can say.

01:22:55.270 --> 01:22:58.820
So I think I agree with you
entirely but I think that,

01:23:02.004 --> 01:23:04.770
but there is a solution.

01:23:04.770 --> 01:23:07.160
It can be institutional,
there's maybe one last question,

01:23:07.160 --> 01:23:08.590
if you don't mind.

01:23:08.590 --> 01:23:09.423
Yes.

01:23:12.158 --> 01:23:16.743
- [Woman 4] (indistinct)
out of time but maybe.

01:23:17.762 --> 01:23:21.095
(indistinct chattering)

01:23:25.320 --> 01:23:26.780
Yeah, please go ahead, (indistinct)

01:23:26.780 --> 01:23:30.947
(laughing)
That's a very powerful.

01:23:32.195 --> 01:23:33.505
(indistinct chattering)

01:23:33.505 --> 01:23:35.755
(laughing)

01:23:41.240 --> 01:23:44.170
- Yes my name is Sarah Caremi.

01:23:44.170 --> 01:23:46.430
I am a film director from Afghanistan.

01:23:46.430 --> 01:23:48.320
I am just visiting (indistinct)

01:23:48.320 --> 01:23:50.890
like visiting small professor

01:23:50.890 --> 01:23:53.480
and also visiting for maker here

01:23:53.480 --> 01:23:56.090
from very far of Afghanistan.

01:23:56.090 --> 01:23:59.410
But accidentally, I just
entered to your class

01:23:59.410 --> 01:24:02.980
because we are preparing for
this screening of my film

01:24:02.980 --> 01:24:06.010
and I just catch few, few sentences.

01:24:06.010 --> 01:24:09.870
I would like to ask Mr. Professor that

01:24:09.870 --> 01:24:12.080
I am come from this country,

01:24:12.080 --> 01:24:15.960
that unfortunately we
have many, many problems.

01:24:15.960 --> 01:24:18.380
Like we have problems, ethical problems.

01:24:18.380 --> 01:24:20.530
We have problems, political problems,

01:24:20.530 --> 01:24:23.360
and everything is so complicated.

01:24:23.360 --> 01:24:27.080
And America, 20 years ago came to country

01:24:27.080 --> 01:24:31.240
with this big slogan that we
are going to solve your issues.

01:24:31.240 --> 01:24:34.450
We are going to motivate you to be United.

01:24:34.450 --> 01:24:36.830
We are going to save your country

01:24:36.830 --> 01:24:39.530
because you have many, many issues.

01:24:39.530 --> 01:24:44.290
And during last 20 years, we
were practicing being United

01:24:44.290 --> 01:24:47.480
and my generation, we were quite good,

01:24:47.480 --> 01:24:50.470
and we were very, very active participant.

01:24:50.470 --> 01:24:54.000
And today I am in America and I am here,

01:24:54.000 --> 01:24:56.310
I am showcasing my films.

01:24:56.310 --> 01:25:01.270
I am showcasing those
achievements that we achieved

01:25:01.270 --> 01:25:03.150
during past 20 years in a country

01:25:03.150 --> 01:25:07.920
that somehow signed a peace
deal with the most terror group

01:25:07.920 --> 01:25:10.810
in the world with the most
ideologist group in the world

01:25:10.810 --> 01:25:14.220
with the most pro ethnic
group in the world

01:25:14.220 --> 01:25:18.480
and somehow by this
still, they divided us.

01:25:18.480 --> 01:25:21.950
They divided my generation,
they divided my country.

01:25:21.950 --> 01:25:26.280
They put new, new and very
old conflict between us.

01:25:26.280 --> 01:25:29.960
What do you think about the
policy America about us,

01:25:29.960 --> 01:25:32.040
about my country and many countries

01:25:32.040 --> 01:25:35.323
that America is now trying to divide it?

01:25:36.686 --> 01:25:37.519
Thank you.

01:25:38.820 --> 01:25:42.370
- So I have, I'm tempted to say

01:25:42.370 --> 01:25:44.610
that's a very, very complicated question,

01:25:44.610 --> 01:25:48.203
which is a bit above my pedigree.

01:25:50.230 --> 01:25:54.140
All I can say is that I wish
the best for Afghanistan

01:25:55.340 --> 01:26:00.340
and for all the countries that
have similar set of issues

01:26:00.970 --> 01:26:05.970
and as a research
community, I'm pretty sure

01:26:07.400 --> 01:26:09.020
we have to contribute to thinking

01:26:09.020 --> 01:26:11.970
about how could Afghanistan

01:26:11.970 --> 01:26:14.290
have been dealt with differently.

01:26:14.290 --> 01:26:19.280
So I think Roger Meison
has a paper on that

01:26:19.280 --> 01:26:24.280
using the experience of British
colonialism indirect rule,

01:26:26.510 --> 01:26:29.950
by saying maybe there was a better way

01:26:29.950 --> 01:26:34.950
to deal with the country, I don't know.

01:26:37.950 --> 01:26:41.610
So the point of
(indistinct) open question.

01:26:41.610 --> 01:26:44.980
So I feel sorry that it's what it is,

01:26:44.980 --> 01:26:49.707
but hopefully we can get
out of the current crisis.

01:26:52.880 --> 01:26:53.713
Thank you.

01:26:55.790 --> 01:26:58.487
- And please join me and thanking Leonard

01:26:58.487 --> 01:26:59.846
